At 390, .blurb hidden. Title controls visible with keyboard hints + touch hint; the touch-only hint is likely displayed only on coarse pointer. Playwright viewport resize doesn't emulate touch, so touch-only is hidden. On real mobile it would show all keyboard hints plus touch line. Need to hide keyboard-specific spans on coarse pointer and show only touch line, or better replace entire title controls content on coarse with touch instructions.

CSS:
```
@media (hover:none) and (pointer:coarse) {
  .title-controls span:not(.touch-only) { display:none; }
  .touch-only { display:inline; }
}
```
And currently `.touch-only` presumably display:none by default. Let's check.

